course: dictionary
lesson: 2972
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Drumstick can mean a stick for hitting a drum, a piece of cooked chicken, or a long green vegetable in some places. Read the words around it to find out which one fits.
explain: «Pizza, sandwiches, chips and chicken drumsticks are finger foods, and most other foods are eaten with cutlery.» The words chicken, finger foods and cutlery are the clues. Cutlery means knives and forks, so a drumstick here must be food you eat with your hands, not a stick.
explain: In a music lesson, the clues are different. Pupils play drums with drumsticks to keep the beat. Drums and beat tell you the word means a stick. Try each meaning in the sentence and choose the one that still makes sense.
fact: A word that has more than one meaning is a word with several possible meanings.
fact: «Drumstick» can mean a stick used to hit a drum.
fact: «Drumstick» can also mean the lower part of a chicken or turkey leg, cooked and eaten.
fact: In some places, «drumstick» means a long green vegetable, the pod of the moringa tree.
fact: «Birds are living dinosaurs: so the drumstick on your plate really is a dinosaur leg.»
exercise: In music lessons, pupils play drums with drumsticks to keep the beat. What does drumstick mean here? | A small drum | The lower leg of a chicken, cooked and eaten | *A stick used to hit a drum | A long green vegetable
exercise: «Chicken drumsticks are a common meal.» What does drumstick mean here? | A long green pod from a tree | A stick for keeping the beat | A pair of music sticks | *The lower part of a chicken leg, cooked and eaten
exercise: «Pizza, sandwiches, chips and chicken drumsticks are finger foods.» Which clue tells you drumstick is food here? | The word beat | The word drums | *The words chicken and finger foods | The word music
test: «She bought a pair of drumsticks for her drum kit.» What does drumstick mean in this sentence? | A cooked chicken leg | A long green vegetable | *A stick used to hit a drum | A bird's wing
test: In some places, drumstick is a long green vegetable. What is the pod of the moringa tree? | A part of a chicken leg | A stick for hitting a drum | A type of dinosaur | *Drumstick, the long green vegetable
exam: «Birds are living dinosaurs, so the drumstick on your plate really is a dinosaur leg.» What does drumstick mean in this sentence? | A long green vegetable | A dinosaur's tail | *The lower part of a chicken leg, cooked and eaten | A stick used to hit a drum
